#! /bin/bash
#
# tools/check_plugin_ui — CI guard for ADR 0035 (embedded basic plugin UI).
#
# Fails if the plugin UI layer (src/plugin/ui) depends on the Qt-Widgets GUI
# application. This is the "done-when" gate for proposal 0006 phase UI-1
# (TU1.3): the basic plugin UI is self-contained Dear ImGui, and a plugin
# must never claim GUI-application ownership inside a host process.
#
# Two hard bans:
#   1. no Qt application object beyond the QCoreApplication that
#      HydrogenPlugin::ensureQtApplication() already owns — QApplication
#      (Qt Widgets) and QGuiApplication (Qt Gui) both take over display
#      connection / session management that belongs to the host, not us;
#   2. no includes from the GUI application tree (src/gui) — the full
#      editor (Qt Widgets, HydrogenApp) must not leak into the plugin UI.
#
# No allowlist: every hit is a design violation, not a convenience.
#
# Copyright(c) 2008-2026 The hydrogen development team [hydrogen-devel@lists.sourceforge.net]
#
# http://www.hydrogen-music.org
#
